IMPORT prelude

-- Legal Identity of Defendants (Organisational Child Abuse) Act 2018 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH), no daydate.
-- Two clocks:
--   * the Act's own 120 days (ss 7(3), 8(1)(a)): plain days, the day of commencement excluded (the reading of the
--     Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Vic) s 44, which is not deposited; READING in NOTES.md);
--   * the Supreme Court (General Civil Procedure) Rules 2025's 7 and 28 days (rr 85.02(2), 85.03), counted under
--     r 3.01 (the day of the event excluded, the last day included; a last day on which the office is closed moves to
--     the next open day), r 3.04 (24 December to 9 January excluded) and r 3.05(2) (a document served after 4 pm or
--     on a day the office is closed is taken as served on the next open day). r 3.08: the office is closed on
--     Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays. Public holidays are not deposited and are not applied (NOTES.md).
--   Rules text: subjects/au/vic/supreme-court-general-civil-procedure-rules-2025/registers/source-bundle/, lines
--   162-185 (rr 3.01-3.05), 195-198 (r 3.08). IMPORT cannot reach another subject, so they are restated here.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from plain-text conversions by Legalese Commons of Word files saved by hand, not the
-- authorised versions. (c) State of Victoria; published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of
-- Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's
-- ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`plain days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is after` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `a` `to` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `b` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `a`

-- DATE_SERIAL counts so that 1 January 1900, a Monday, is 693960, which leaves 1 when divided by 7 (checked: 2 November
-- 2026, a Monday, is 740286, which also leaves 1). So a remainder of 6 is a Saturday and 0 a Sunday.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Saturday or Sunday` `the day` IF
        (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) EQUALS 6
    OR  (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) EQUALS 0

-- r 3.04(1): "the period from 24 December to 9 January next following shall be excluded".
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in the Christmas vacation` `the day` IF
        (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT LEAST 24)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST 9)

-- r 3.01(5), r 3.08: the day itself if the office is open, otherwise the next day it is open (weekends only).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first open day on or after` `the day` MEANS
    IF `is a Saturday or Sunday` `the day`
    THEN `the first open day on or after` (`plain days after` 1 `the day`)
    ELSE `the day`

-- r 3.05(2): a document served after 4 pm, or on a day the office is closed, is taken as served on the next open day.
GIVEN `the day served` IS A DATE, `after 4 pm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the day taken as served` `the day served` `after 4 pm` MEANS
    IF `after 4 pm`
    THEN `the first open day on or after` (`plain days after` 1 `the day served`)
    ELSE `the first open day on or after` `the day served`

-- r 3.01(2), r 3.04(1): count n days from a day, the day excluded, skipping 24 December to 9 January.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`rules days after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    IF `n` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `is in the Christmas vacation` (`plain days after` 1 `the day`)
         THEN `rules days after` `n` (`plain days after` 1 `the day`)
         ELSE `rules days after` (`n` MINUS 1) (`plain days after` 1 `the day`)

-- The last day for an act the Rules give n days for, counted from a day: rr 3.01(2), (5), 3.04(1), 3.08.
-- r 3.01(4) (closed days excluded from a period of 5 days or less) does not reach the 7 and 28 days encoded here.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day under the Rules` `n` `the day` MEANS `the first open day on or after` (`rules days after` `n` `the day`)
